      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
        Cairo International Airport overview
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        Cairo International Airport (CAI) is the primary aviation gateway to Egypt and the second busiest airport in Africa. Situated in the historic district of Heliopolis, approximately 15 kilometers (9 miles) northeast of central Cairo, the airport features three commercial passenger terminals (Terminal 1, Terminal 2, and the modern Terminal 3) linked by an Automated People Mover (APM).
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Navigating CAI after arrival is straightforward when you have a pre-booked driver. After passport control, baggage claim, and customs inspection, you will enter the public arrivals hall where your designated chauffeur will be waiting with your name displayed.
      </p>
